WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.640
- Speaking of running for office,

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.130
there's a game on the web right now

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.580
to figure out your personal
presidential campaign slogan.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.413
I love it.

00:00:07.413 --> 00:00:10.900
It's your name, the year you
want to run for president,

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.021
and the last thing you texted.

00:00:13.021 --> 00:00:13.854
(audience laughs)

00:00:13.854 --> 00:00:14.970
So, I feel like it works.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.170
Mine, and I figured
this out before the show

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.373
and it's awesome,

00:00:19.411 --> 00:00:21.460
mine is Clarkson 2028,

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.440
oh shoot, you actually just reminded me

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.680
that Cassie texted me,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.800
and I never got back to her.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.700
I'm such an ass.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.470
Please tell her I'm so sorry,

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.281
I just remembered, grimace face.

00:00:30.281 --> 00:00:31.114
(laughs)

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:33.767
Its like, that's my slogan. (laughs)

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:34.600
(clapping)

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.640
Well, what is yours?

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.400
- I brought out my phone.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.917
- I was like, beforehand I was like,

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:40.721
"I cannot believe this is my last text."

00:00:40.721 --> 00:00:41.850
(laughs)

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.136
- Actually I just, I texted Cab,

00:00:44.136 --> 00:00:47.500
because I was actually sending
him the first two episodes,

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.040
'cause he gets extra, first.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.282
So I just went, "Just for you, baby."

00:00:51.282 --> 00:00:52.115
(laughs loudly)

00:00:52.115 --> 00:00:55.578
It'd be like, Dawson
2028, just for you baby.

00:00:55.578 --> 00:00:56.880
(audience laughs)

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:57.713
(clapping)

00:00:57.713 --> 00:00:58.745
- That's actually awesome!

00:00:58.745 --> 00:01:00.871
- It sounds a little bit,

00:01:00.871 --> 00:01:02.230
I remember being at the Met Ball

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:04.160
and Rihanna was performing

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.620
and then the surprise
guest was Kanye West,

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.320
and he came out and everyone
got super excited to see him

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.870
and the first thing,
he walks up to the mic

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.520
with all this like rounding applause,

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:16.304
and the first thing he
says is, "You're welcome."

00:01:16.304 --> 00:01:17.137
- Oh my god.

00:01:17.137 --> 00:01:17.970
- And I was like, "You know, he's talking

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:18.957
"about running for office,

00:01:18.957 --> 00:01:20.710
"and I think that should
be his campaign slogan."

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:21.543
- [Kelly] You're welcome.

00:01:21.543 --> 00:01:23.920
- Kanye West for
president, you're welcome.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.700
- I actually say that a lot myself,

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.870
so I can't make fun (laughs) of him.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:28.780
Usually I'm like, "You're welcome."

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.380
But it's usually when I mess up.

